(Bug #51's siblings. The register found the declaration form, but the same
 cast-free write lands in a text slot four other ways, and every one of
 them stored the buffer's struct pointer and printed the capacity byte.
 `Set` and `the ... is` were refused outright by the type lock, which
 named a cast that would not have changed what the sentence meant; under
 the owner's ruling they convert instead, exactly as the declaration does.

 The one code path is `emit_buffer_to_text_copy`, so this file is really
 asking whether every site reaches it.)

To 'echo the text' with a text called what. Print what.
To 'hand back a text' with a buffer called source. Return a text, source.

a buffer called label is 64 bytes in size.
append "first" to label.

(`Set t to <buffer>`)
a text called assigned is "seed".
Set assigned to label.
Print assigned.

(`the t is <buffer>`)
a text called restated is "seed".
the restated is label.
Print restated.

(a text parameter receiving a buffer argument)
'echo the text' with label.

(`Return a text, <buffer>`)
a text called returned is 'hand back a text' with label.
Print returned.
